From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 19:39:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] script: Delay the load event while web fonts are loading

A web font is only fetched once layout finds text that needs it, so nothing
kept the load event from firing before the fonts a page uses had loaded.
`load` event handlers that measure text, like the ones in check-layout-th.js
tests, then saw the fallback font. Chrome and Firefox also only load the fonts
a page uses, and css/css-flexbox/flex-item-compressible-001.html passes in both.

While any web font is loading after a reflow, the document now holds a load
blocker, which is released once the loads have been applied to the page. To
let fonts that newly loaded stylesheets need take part, the document lays out
pending changes before it stops waiting for load blockers.

Fork note: fixes a regression from "fonts: Only load @font-face fonts that the
page uses", but is meant for upstream on its own: with eager loading the same
race existed, the font download just usually won it.

Testing: css/css-flexbox/flex-item-compressible-001.html,
css/css-grid/subgrid/subgrid-baseline-016.html and -018.html,
css/css-grid/alignment/self-baseline/grid-self-baseline-two-dimensional.html
and css/cssom-view/offsetTopLeft-border-box.html pass again, and five subtests
of css/css-flexbox/text-as-flexitem-size-001.html now pass.

Validation: `./mach test-wpt --release css/css-fonts css/css-font-loading css/css-flexbox css/css-grid css/cssom-view html/canvas/element/text html/canvas/offscreen/text` (4921 tests): the text-as-flexitem-size-001 subtests pass in 5 of 5 repeats (0 of 5 without this patch); the only other unexpected results are font-variant-emoji-1 FAIL (also on plain ohos-main) and the known intermittent grid-self-alignment-fit-content-001 (servo/servo#47515).
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; root-caused from the servo-ohos PR 12 try run and written by the agent)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
